LICENSING FOR THE ORDER-18 LEECH-TREE COMPUTER-ASSISTED PROOF

This repository uses different licenses for different categories of material.
The licenses are assigned by the role of a file, not merely by its filename
extension. They are not alternative licenses for the same material.

1. SOFTWARE: APACHE LICENSE 2.0

Unless a file is identified as third-party material or carries a different
license notice, project-authored software is licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (SPDX identifier: Apache-2.0). This category includes:

* Lean source files and formalization software;
* C and C++ source and header files;
* Python source files;
* shell, PowerShell, batch, build, orchestration, and verification scripts;
* project-authored solver and verifier software, in source or executable form;
* build-system and machine-readable configuration files whose primary purpose
  is to build, run, test, or verify that software.

The complete terms are in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt and at
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.

2. RESEARCH MATERIALS: CREATIVE COMMONS ATTRIBUTION 4.0 INTERNATIONAL

Unless a file is identified as third-party material or carries a different
license notice, project-authored non-software research materials are licensed
under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International Public License
(SPDX identifier: CC-BY-4.0). This category includes:

* computational evidence and preserved search results;
* input and output data, partition plans, and partition-root data;
* certificates, receipts, logs, transcripts, manifests, and result records;
* documentation, mathematical exposition, catalogues, and metadata; and
* figures, diagrams, and other visual material.

The complete terms are in LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt and at
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.

For attribution, cite the work as "Order-18 Leech-tree computer-assisted
proof," credit the LeechTrees research contributors, identify the version or
commit used, link to the public source when one exists, and indicate whether
changes were made.

3. SCOPE RULES AND EXCEPTIONS

* File-level license notices take precedence over this repository-level map.
* A project-authored source-code file remains Apache-2.0 even when preserved
  inside an evidence or archival directory.
* Documentation and evidentiary records remain CC-BY-4.0 even when located
  beside software.
* A machine-readable file used as executable/build configuration is
  Apache-2.0; a machine-readable file recording inputs, outputs, provenance,
  receipts, manifests, or results is CC-BY-4.0.
* A mixed archive or Git bundle is not assigned one blanket license. Each
  contained file follows these rules after extraction.
* The text of the license files is supplied as the applicable legal text and
  is not itself relicensed by this notice.
* These grants apply only to material for which the applicable rights holders
  have authority to grant the stated license. Third-party components retain
  their own copyright and license terms. In particular, the retained MinGW
  runtime DLLs are excluded from these project licenses. See
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
* Trademarks, personal data, privacy rights, and rights of publicity are not
  licensed except to the extent expressly provided by the applicable license.

Copyright in individual contributions remains with the applicable copyright
holders.
